## Summary

The `OpenBISModel.ts` file defines TypeScript interfaces for openBIS entities, but they're incomplete compared to the actual API responses. Complete type definitions are essential for type-safe API integration in Phase 1, ensuring all properties are properly typed and discoverable.

## Source Location

**File:** `lib/model/OpenBISModel.ts`
**Line:** 45

## Current Code Context

```typescript
// TODO: fully implement OpenBIS types and extensions for each type
// FEAT: add zod schemas for validation of json-rpc output
export interface OpenbisEntityBase {
  kind: OpenbisEntityKind;
  permId: OpenbisPermId;
  code: string;
  registrationDate: Date;
  modificationDate: Date;
  registratedBy: OpenbisUser;
  frozen?: boolean;
  description?: string | null;
}

export interface OpenbisSpace extends OpenbisEntityBase {
  kind: "SPACE";
  frozenForProjects?: boolean;
  frozenForObjects?: boolean;
}
// ... other entity interfaces
```

## Analysis

Current entity definitions cover:
- ✅ Basic identification (permId, code, kind)
- ✅ Timestamps (registration, modification dates)
- ✅ User references (registratedBy)
- ✅ Frozen states
- ✅ Basic relationships (projectIdentifier, etc.)

Missing from openBIS API:
- ❌ Properties bag (dynamic properties based on entity type)
- ❌ Attachments
- ❌ History tracking fields
- ❌ Metadata store references
- ❌ Sample/dataset links for experiments
- ❌ Physical/link dataset specific fields
- ❌ Space role assignments

Key challenges:
1. openBIS uses dynamic typing for properties (varies by object type)
2. Relationships can be fetched at different depths
3. Some fields are only present with specific fetch options

## Suggested Implementation

1. **Document API response structure**
   - Capture actual JSON responses from openBIS API
   - Document required vs optional fields
   - Note fetch-option-dependent fields

2. **Extend base interface**
   ```typescript
   export interface OpenbisEntityBase {
     // ... existing fields ...

     // Properties (type-specific key-value pairs)
     properties?: Record<string, unknown>;

     // Attachments
     attachments?: OpenbisAttachment[];

     // Metadata
     metaData?: Record<string, string>;
   }
   ```

3. **Complete entity-specific interfaces**
   ```typescript
   export interface OpenbisObject extends OpenbisEntityBase {
     kind: "OBJECT";
     // ... existing fields ...

     // Sample-specific
     space?: OpenbisSpace;
     project?: OpenbisProject;
     experiment?: OpenbisCollection;
     properties: Record<string, unknown>;
     sampleType: OpenbisObjectType;

     // Relationships
     parents?: OpenbisObject[];
     children?: OpenbisObject[];
     container?: OpenbisObject;
     components?: OpenbisObject[];
     datasets?: OpenbisDataset[];
   }
   ```

4. **Add helper types**
   ```typescript
   export interface OpenbisAttachment {
     fileName: string;
     title: string;
     description?: string;
     version: number;
   }

   export interface OpenbisObjectType {
     code: string;
     description?: string;
     propertyAssignments: OpenbisPropertyAssignment[];
   }
   ```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] All entity interfaces match openBIS API responses
- [ ] Properties bag properly typed (Record with known keys where possible)
- [ ] Relationship types support nested entities
- [ ] Optional fields correctly marked
- [ ] JSDoc comments for complex fields
- [ ] No `any` types used
- [ ] Code passes linting and type checks
- [ ] TODO comment removed after implementation

